    {
      "noteId": "wis-5-5-first-kaf",
      "book": "WIS",
      "chapter": 5,
      "verse": 5,
      "anchorBefore": "איככָה",
      "letterIndex": 3,
      "decision": "retireNote",
      "finding": "The first Kaf body reaches the common baseline near1626. Below that baseline is a new broad horizontal bar at1634..1648, followed by a narrower central stem continuing to1684. The attached point has the complete bar-plus-long-stem Qamats geometry. The very next physical Kaf, already transcribed with Qamats, independently has the same pattern: new broad bar near1638..1647 and narrower stem to1680. The corresponding upper letter bodies are distinct, so this is a same-letter literal control rather than a repeated-word substitution. The clear long lower stem excludes the flat Patah comparator and does not form a simple two-round-node Sheva.",
